From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:36:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] board: mediatek-mobile: take the serial number from
 /firmware/android

LK publishes the proinfo serial number for Android as
/firmware/android/serialno in the FDT it passes; androidboot.serialno is
in the bootconfig, not the bootargs. Prefer that property so fastboot
and the USB iSerial descriptor report the device's serial number.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
index 78a99c9bf9e..f9d9e18c543 100644
--- a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
+++ b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
@@ -627,7 +627,18 @@ static void mtk_set_serial(void)
 	const void *fdt = (const void *)(uintptr_t)mtk_lk_fdt;
 	const char *bootargs = NULL, *value, *end;
 	char serial[65];
-	int node;
+	int node, len;
+
+	/* LK publishes the proinfo serial number for Android here. */
+	node = fdt_path_offset(fdt, "/firmware/android");
+	if (node >= 0) {
+		value = fdt_getprop(fdt, node, "serialno", &len);
+		if (value && len > 1 && len <= sizeof(serial) &&
+		    strnlen(value, len) == len - 1) {
+			env_set("serial#", value);
+			return;
+		}
+	}
 
 	node = fdt_path_offset(fdt, "/chosen");
 	if (node >= 0)
-- 
